DevOps Engineers are pivotal in automating and streamlining the software development lifecycle. 
They construct and oversee CI/CD pipelines utilizing tools such as GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, and Ansible. 
Serving as the link between development and operations teams, their objective is to deliver software efficiently, consistently, and with minimal errors.

Site Reliability Engineers (SRE) blend software engineering with operations, prioritizing reliability and uptime. 
They monitor performance, establish alerts, and guarantee system availability using tools like Grafana, Datadog, Prometheus, and Splunk. 
By defining and managing SLOs, SLAs, and SLIs, they strive to maintain seamless system operations with high availability and reliability.

Cloud Engineers focus on crafting, constructing, and upholding cloud infrastructure across platforms like Azure, AWS, and GCP. 
Their responsibilities encompass managing virtual networks, storage, compute resources, and cloud security. 
By utilizing tools like Terraform, Ansible, and Kubernetes, they ensure optimal performance, cost efficiency, and adherence to security protocols to develop scalable, secure, and economically viable cloud environments.
